Yes, sure. Let's plan ahead for the big slippery slope. ;-)

I'm just suggesting the spellbook thing, nothing more. Even your potion step
is too much in my opinion. Potions seem more chemical than magical to me.

The words in spellbooks are a limited resource. Eventually, they will
disappear from your head. If you read a book too often, it will fade. Seems
to me those books have a store of magical energy (like in the Discworld
novels) that you should be able to drain by putting them in direct contact
with an anti-magic field.

That's _direct contact_, so items in your inventory are not at risk.

I understand the concerns about implementability. But nethack code seems
sensibly written to me. I don't think it would be that much trouble. As for
consistency, I don't see any other aspects that have to be changed to keep
the game consistent. Ok, whether the trick would also work on scrolls could
be a point of discussion.

By the way, I never actually expected my feature to be implemented in the
game. It's just fun to discuss these things.

